WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:02.133
-The investigation

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:04.300
into former President Trump's
attempted coup

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:06.000
took a truly stunning turn
this week

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.734
when it was revealed
that his own son Don Jr.,

00:00:08.734 --> 00:00:10.467
as well as several
Fox News hosts,

00:00:10.467 --> 00:00:12.367
privately begged
Trump's chief of staff

00:00:12.367 --> 00:00:15.033
to get Trump to stop the attack
on the Capitol.

00:00:15.033 --> 00:00:16.701
And yet, in public,
those same people

00:00:16.701 --> 00:00:18.868
defended Trump and lied
about the insurrection.

00:00:18.868 --> 00:00:21.167
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:21.167 --> 00:00:25.400
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:28.467
On Monday, on this very show,
we did a "Closer Look"

00:00:28.467 --> 00:00:29.801
where we laid out
everything we knew

00:00:29.801 --> 00:00:31.067
about the coup attempt that led

00:00:31.067 --> 00:00:32.467
to the January 6th insurrection

00:00:32.467 --> 00:00:34.667
and said that,
every time you think

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:36.934
it can't get more shocking,
it does.

00:00:36.934 --> 00:00:38.634
We taped that segment
Monday afternoon

00:00:38.634 --> 00:00:40.534
and, before it even aired later
that night,

00:00:40.534 --> 00:00:42.968
more shocking
revelations emerged.

00:00:42.968 --> 00:00:45.300
Soon, we're just going to have
to leave a space in the show

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:49.167
where I move my mouth so we can
digitally insert words later.

00:00:49.167 --> 00:00:50.767
[ Laughter ]
You know, like this --

00:00:50.767 --> 00:00:53.234
-Donald Trump held a séance
at the White House

00:00:53.234 --> 00:00:55.267
to contact the ghost
of Benjamin Franklin

00:00:55.267 --> 00:00:57.300
to ask him
to overturn the election.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.367
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.367 --> 00:01:01.000
-It's not perfect,
but it's pretty good.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:02.767
[ Laughter and applause ]
The investigation took

00:01:02.767 --> 00:01:04.267
yet another stunning turn
this week,

00:01:04.267 --> 00:01:06.801
when we learned that prominent
Trump supporters on Fox News

00:01:06.801 --> 00:01:09.400
and even his own son,
who have spent almost a year

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:11.601
minimizing or lying to us
about what happened on that day,

00:01:11.601 --> 00:01:13.667
were privately pleading
with Trump's chief of staff,

00:01:13.667 --> 00:01:16.901
Mark Meadows, during the attack,
to get Trump to put a stop to it

00:01:16.901 --> 00:01:19.000
and telling him what they
actually thought of it --

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:21.167
that it was really, really bad.

00:01:21.167 --> 00:01:24.067
-The evidence that the
January 6th Committee
laid out tonight

00:01:24.067 --> 00:01:26.734
against former White House
Chief of Staff Mark Meadows

00:01:26.734 --> 00:01:28.167
was truly extraordinary

00:01:28.167 --> 00:01:31.033
and it was all evidence
that Mark Meadows himself

00:01:31.033 --> 00:01:33.567
turned over to the committee,
at his own will.

00:01:33.567 --> 00:01:36.367
That evidence showed that a slew
of Fox News hosts,

00:01:36.367 --> 00:01:38.467
from Laura Ingraham
to Sean Hannity,

00:01:38.467 --> 00:01:43.300
were begging Mark Meadows to get
Donald Trump to stop the siege,

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:45.434
and he refused.
-Text messages

00:01:45.434 --> 00:01:48.100
to former White House
Chief of Staff Mark Meadows

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:51.701
from Donald Trump Jr.,
from Fox entertainers,

00:01:51.701 --> 00:01:53.367
from Trump
administration officials,

00:01:53.367 --> 00:01:56.167
even from some lawmakers,
that all privately

00:01:56.167 --> 00:01:59.567
and, for a time,
unsuccessfully, beg

00:01:59.567 --> 00:02:01.868
to do something
to stop the violence

00:02:01.868 --> 00:02:03.868
as the attack unfolded
at the Capitol.

00:02:03.868 --> 00:02:06.167
-Damn, they have Don Jr.'s
text messages

00:02:06.167 --> 00:02:08.467
to his father's chief of staff,
which means

00:02:08.467 --> 00:02:11.534
Don Jr. doesn't have
his father's own phone number?

00:02:11.534 --> 00:02:14.267
[ Laughter ]
And, if Don Jr. gets relegated

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:15.367
to the chief of staff,

00:02:15.367 --> 00:02:18.200
who does Eric have
to go through, Rudy?

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:19.334
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:31.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:34.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.634 --> 00:02:36.701
Whatever else we find out
about the actual texts,

00:02:36.701 --> 00:02:37.901
there's nothing
more embarrassing

00:02:37.901 --> 00:02:39.367
than not having
your dad's number.

00:02:39.367 --> 00:02:40.868
That would be like
if I only communicated

00:02:40.868 --> 00:02:42.334
with my dad through Wally.

00:02:42.334 --> 00:02:45.701
Oh, by the way, Wally, what did
he think of the show last night?

00:02:45.701 --> 00:02:48.701
Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:50.300
Did he say anything else?

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:51.767
-Seth, I just print
what he tells me.

00:02:51.767 --> 00:02:52.834
[ Laughter ]
-Alright.

00:02:52.834 --> 00:02:54.534
Even Kendall Roy gets to talk

00:02:54.534 --> 00:02:55.801
face-to-face with Logan,

00:02:55.801 --> 00:02:57.367
although, it's usually
just something like --

00:02:57.367 --> 00:02:58.567
[ As Kendall ]
Uh...

00:02:58.567 --> 00:02:59.901
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.901 --> 00:03:02.100
Dad.

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:03.734
I've been doing that impression
for like three months now

00:03:03.734 --> 00:03:05.801
and I feel like it gets
marginally better every time.

00:03:05.801 --> 00:03:07.501
[ Laughter ]
I did it on this show

00:03:07.501 --> 00:03:09.367
for the Brian Cox,
who plays Logan,

00:03:09.367 --> 00:03:11.133
and the nicest thing
he could say about it --

00:03:11.133 --> 00:03:13.400
and this is verbatim --
was that it was

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:14.901
"incredibly brief."

00:03:14.901 --> 00:03:17.400
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:19.133
But I took that as a challenge
and I think, now,

00:03:19.133 --> 00:03:20.133
I can stretch
the impression out.

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:21.267
Here's my Kendall Roy,

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:23.501
if he was planning
the Capitol insurrection,

00:03:23.501 --> 00:03:25.234
[ As Kendall ]
I say we [bleep]
storm the place,

00:03:25.234 --> 00:03:27.501
[ Laughter ]
go full [bleep] Visigoth,
you know,

00:03:27.501 --> 00:03:29.367
ancient Rome,
end of the world [bleep],

00:03:29.367 --> 00:03:32.567
get some Silicon [bleep] Valley
tech [bleep]

00:03:32.567 --> 00:03:35.467
[ Laughter and applause ]
to generate some
social buzz for us,

00:03:35.467 --> 00:03:38.667
maybe a big [bleep]
with a Viking helmet
fur [bleep] hat,

00:03:38.667 --> 00:03:40.734
[ Laughter and applause ]
get in there and jack a podium
or some [bleep]

00:03:40.734 --> 00:03:41.968
Make it [bleep]

00:03:41.968 --> 00:03:43.567
I don't know. Whatever.
What do you say, Greg?

00:03:43.567 --> 00:03:45.400
[ As Greg ]
Uh, wow. It, uh,

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:47.067
[ Laughter and applause ]
seems --

00:03:47.067 --> 00:03:48.901
it seems great, but, uh, also,

00:03:48.901 --> 00:03:50.133
maybe illegal?

00:03:50.133 --> 00:03:53.367
And, um, Tom said that,
if I get involved

00:03:53.367 --> 00:03:57.467
in anything extrajudicial, um,

00:03:57.467 --> 00:03:59.000
he would make me, uh...

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:00.400
[ Laughter ]

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:01.767
...eat a big bucket of [bleep]

00:04:01.767 --> 00:04:03.100
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:04.901
So it turns out a bunch
of Fox News hosts

00:04:04.901 --> 00:04:08.334
and Trump's own son sent urgent,
pleading text messages

00:04:08.334 --> 00:04:09.467
to Trump's chief of staff

00:04:09.467 --> 00:04:10.934
as the insurrection
was unfolding,

00:04:10.934 --> 00:04:13.367
begging him to tell Trump
to do something about it.

00:04:13.367 --> 00:04:16.033
And, just so you know,
I don't text or communicate

00:04:16.033 --> 00:04:17.834
in any way with politicians,
but, if I did,

00:04:17.834 --> 00:04:19.334
it would be
to tell Chuck Schumer

00:04:19.334 --> 00:04:22.200
to push his glasses up!
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:24.767
I don't care how salient
a point you're making, my man.

00:04:24.767 --> 00:04:26.701
When those bad boys are dangling
on your nose tip,

00:04:26.701 --> 00:04:28.601
all I can think is
they're going to fall off

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:30.367
and he's going to need to buy
a new pair of glasses.

00:04:30.367 --> 00:04:31.868
[ Laughter ]
But the bombshells kept coming

00:04:31.868 --> 00:04:33.567
when Wyoming
Congresswoman Liz Cheney

00:04:33.567 --> 00:04:34.834
read the texts during a hearing

00:04:34.834 --> 00:04:37.167
on whether to hold Meadows
in contempt on Monday.

00:04:37.167 --> 00:04:42.167
-According to the records,
multiple Fox News hosts

00:04:42.167 --> 00:04:46.000
knew the president needed
to act immediately.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:48.100
They texted Mr. Meadows

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:51.734
and he has turned over
those texts.

00:04:51.734 --> 00:04:54.901
"Mark, the president needs

00:04:54.901 --> 00:04:58.167
to tell people in the Capitol
to go home.

00:04:58.167 --> 00:05:00.267
This is hurting all of us.

00:05:00.267 --> 00:05:04.400
He is destroying his legacy,"
Laura Ingraham wrote.

00:05:05.834 --> 00:05:08.534
"Please get him on TV.

00:05:08.534 --> 00:05:11.801
Destroying everything
you have accomplished,"

00:05:11.801 --> 00:05:14.567
Brian Kilmeade texted.

00:05:14.567 --> 00:05:17.167
"Can he make a statement?

00:05:17.167 --> 00:05:21.434
Ask people to leave the
Capitol?" Sean Hannity urged.

00:05:22.634 --> 00:05:24.667
As the violence continued,

00:05:24.667 --> 00:05:27.968
one of the president's sons
texted Mr. Meadows,

00:05:27.968 --> 00:05:32.467
"He's got to condemn
this [bleep] asap.

00:05:32.467 --> 00:05:34.901
[ Laughter ]
The capitol police tweet

00:05:34.901 --> 00:05:38.634
is not enough,"
Donald Trump Jr. texted.

00:05:38.634 --> 00:05:40.334
-Man, what else was
in those messages?

00:05:40.334 --> 00:05:42.734
Is there a text from Kilmeade
asking Mark Meadows...

00:05:46.033 --> 00:05:47.701
[ Laughter ]

00:05:47.701 --> 00:05:49.601
Also, were you all
really shocked

00:05:49.601 --> 00:05:51.567
that people were violently
storming the Capitol?

00:05:51.567 --> 00:05:54.801
You're the ones who told them
the election was stolen.

00:05:54.801 --> 00:05:57.767
Hannity was even saying that
on the night of January 6th.

00:05:57.767 --> 00:06:02.000
-83% of Republicans,
almost 30% of independents,

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:06.033
millions of Democrats,
that saw irregularities

00:06:06.033 --> 00:06:07.334
and their strong belief

00:06:07.334 --> 00:06:09.834
the election was,
in fact, fraudulent.

00:06:09.834 --> 00:06:12.367
Our election, frankly,
was a train wreck.

00:06:12.367 --> 00:06:15.701
80% -- 83%, according to Gallup,
of Republicans

00:06:15.701 --> 00:06:17.133
and millions of others

00:06:17.133 --> 00:06:19.868
do not have faith
in these election results.

00:06:19.868 --> 00:06:23.367
You can't just snap your finger
and hope that goes away.

00:06:23.367 --> 00:06:26.567
Make no mistake, there were
serious election irregularities.

00:06:26.567 --> 00:06:27.968
We've got to address them,

00:06:27.968 --> 00:06:30.067
in state after state
after state.

00:06:30.067 --> 00:06:32.934
Why? Because, as a country,
we can't have

00:06:32.934 --> 00:06:36.734
83% of one party,
30% of independents,

00:06:36.734 --> 00:06:39.868
not having confidence
in the election result.

00:06:39.868 --> 00:06:42.000
-Because you told them that!

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:43.033
[ Laughter ]
You can't complain

00:06:43.033 --> 00:06:44.767
about how the subway smells

00:06:44.767 --> 00:06:47.400
when you're the guy that took
a [bleep] on the F train.

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:49.133
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:49.133 --> 00:06:51.100
"I think I might ask
for a refund."

00:06:51.100 --> 00:06:52.267
[ Laughter ]

00:06:52.267 --> 00:06:53.968
You guys fed them lie
after lie

00:06:53.968 --> 00:06:55.534
about election fraud,
despite the fact

00:06:55.534 --> 00:06:57.400
that there was zero evidence
to back it up.

00:06:57.400 --> 00:06:59.267
They lost more
than 60 court cases,

00:06:59.267 --> 00:07:01.434
including in front
of Trump-appointed judges.

00:07:01.434 --> 00:07:04.100
The two-step these guys tried
to pull off,

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:06.467
of telling their viewers
there was fraud,

00:07:06.467 --> 00:07:08.968
when claiming we have
to investigate
that made-up fraud

00:07:08.968 --> 00:07:11.434
because their viewers believe
there was fraud

00:07:11.434 --> 00:07:13.467
is honestly insulting
to everyone's intelligence.

00:07:13.467 --> 00:07:16.133
That's the logic of parents
who tell their kids

00:07:16.133 --> 00:07:17.534
there's a monster
under their bed

00:07:17.534 --> 00:07:19.434
who will come out at night
and eat them,

00:07:19.434 --> 00:07:21.567
if they don't brush their teeth,
then complain

00:07:21.567 --> 00:07:23.200
that their children don't want
to go to bed.

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:24.701
[ Laughter ]
"Look, man, you don't have
to worry. I told you.

00:07:24.701 --> 00:07:26.100
If you brush your teeth,
he won't eat you."

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:28.734
Yeah, but he's still a monster.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:28.734 --> 00:07:31.534
I mean, maybe he doesn't play
by your rules, Dad.

00:07:31.534 --> 00:07:32.734
Plus, he's got
to eat something, right?

00:07:32.734 --> 00:07:34.000
He's just going to go hungry
all night

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:35.033
because I brush my teeth?

00:07:35.033 --> 00:07:36.601
I feel like your theory

00:07:36.601 --> 00:07:37.701
is a little shaky, at best.

00:07:37.701 --> 00:07:39.267
"Oh, my God!
Go to bed!"

00:07:39.267 --> 00:07:41.167
[ Laughter ]
Also, I can't believe

00:07:41.167 --> 00:07:43.968
they naively thought they could
actually get Trump to go on TV

00:07:43.968 --> 00:07:46.167
and condemn the insurrection
he himself whipped up.

00:07:46.167 --> 00:07:47.901
And, in the end, of course,
he ignored them.

00:07:47.901 --> 00:07:49.400
All they could get him to do
was shoot one

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:51.400
of those weird videos in the
White House Rose Garden,

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:53.934
where he looks like he's hosting
a show on Animal Planet,

00:07:53.934 --> 00:07:55.868
exploring the Australian bush.

00:07:55.868 --> 00:07:57.701
[ Aussie accent ]
Welcome, everyone,
to "Wild Adventures."

00:07:57.701 --> 00:08:00.300
We're here looking for the rare
long-footed potoroo

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:01.634
and -- oh, would you look
at that.

00:08:01.634 --> 00:08:04.334
There's a, uh, press secretary
hiding in the bushes.

00:08:04.334 --> 00:08:05.601
[ Laughter ]

00:08:05.601 --> 00:08:08.934
Look at that, Sean Spicer,
old Spizza over there.

00:08:08.934 --> 00:08:11.000
That one's a joke
from a recurring segment.

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:14.067
Remember that?
♪♪

00:08:14.067 --> 00:08:16.567
When the press secretary hid
from reporters in the bushes,

00:08:16.567 --> 00:08:18.000
like a high school sophomore
who just left

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:20.200
a flaming bag of dog turds
on his neighbor's doorstep?

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:22.000
[ Laughter ]
"Oh, [bleep]! He sees us! Run!"

00:08:22.067 --> 00:08:23.834
[ Laughter ]
This has been "Remember That?"

00:08:23.834 --> 00:08:25.033
♪♪

00:08:25.033 --> 00:08:26.567
[ Laughter ]
It's surprising to think that,

00:08:26.567 --> 00:08:29.200
even as close
as these people are to Trump,

00:08:29.200 --> 00:08:30.767
they still don't know
the real him.

00:08:30.767 --> 00:08:34.033
You think he wanted to go on TV
and condemn his own supporters?

00:08:34.033 --> 00:08:36.667
By all accounts,
he was watching the riots on TV

00:08:36.667 --> 00:08:38.033
and, according
to one Republican senator,

00:08:38.033 --> 00:08:39.901
he was excited and delighted
by what he saw.

00:08:39.901 --> 00:08:41.100
The Washington Post reported
that Trump...

00:08:56.367 --> 00:08:57.334
[ Laughter ]

00:08:59.133 --> 00:09:02.434
[ Laughter ]
Someone has to teach him how
to use a DVR.

00:09:02.434 --> 00:09:04.534
I mean, you can pause
live TV now.

00:09:04.534 --> 00:09:06.934
Can we get a Verizon technician
over to Mar-a-Lago?

00:09:06.934 --> 00:09:08.267
"Alright, you're all set, sir."

00:09:08.267 --> 00:09:09.434
[ As Trump ]
And, now, can I talk

00:09:09.434 --> 00:09:10.868
to the people
on the little screen?

00:09:10.868 --> 00:09:13.701
"Nope, nope, they're on TV,
so they can't hear you."

00:09:13.701 --> 00:09:15.133
[ As Trump ]
Okay, but just in case they can,

00:09:15.133 --> 00:09:16.567
is Brian Kilmeade one
of the friends,

00:09:16.567 --> 00:09:19.467
or is he the fox?
[ Laughter ]

00:09:19.467 --> 00:09:20.567
So what were we saying --

00:09:20.567 --> 00:09:22.534
So, now, what these Fox hosts

00:09:22.534 --> 00:09:24.334
were saying privately
about what happened --

00:09:24.334 --> 00:09:26.567
Sorry.
So now, what --

00:09:26.567 --> 00:09:30.133
[ Laughter ]

00:09:30.133 --> 00:09:31.634
Wally.

00:09:31.634 --> 00:09:32.834
Wally, do you know it's wrong?

00:09:32.834 --> 00:09:34.534
-Yeah. Yeah.
-Okay.

00:09:34.534 --> 00:09:36.300
-"So now we what these."

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:38.300
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:40.367 --> 00:09:42.200
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:09:44.868 --> 00:09:45.901
Look at this guy.

00:09:45.901 --> 00:09:47.601
Look at this technical solution.
-Yes.

00:09:47.601 --> 00:09:50.868
[ Laughter ]

00:09:50.868 --> 00:09:53.868
-[ Changes accent ]
Old Two Finger Wally
to the rescue.

00:09:53.868 --> 00:09:55.868
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:57.701 --> 00:09:59.367
So --

00:09:59.367 --> 00:10:01.434
Maybe my dad's next message
will be for you!

00:10:01.434 --> 00:10:02.801
[ Laughter ]

00:10:02.801 --> 00:10:05.167
So, now, what these Fox hosts
were saying privately

00:10:05.167 --> 00:10:07.534
about the reality of what
happened on January 6th.

00:10:07.534 --> 00:10:10.033
In public, though,
on their TV and radio shows,

00:10:10.033 --> 00:10:12.133
they repeatedly went to great
lengths to minimize it,

00:10:12.133 --> 00:10:14.067
to amplify the lies
about election fraud

00:10:14.067 --> 00:10:16.300
that motivated it
and even suggest

00:10:16.300 --> 00:10:17.901
that there may have been
other elements,

00:10:17.901 --> 00:10:20.000
like antifa,
involved in the riot.

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:21.634
-The FBI will infiltrate groups,

00:10:21.634 --> 00:10:23.634
whether it's the mob
or al Qaeda,

00:10:23.634 --> 00:10:25.133
and they'll try
to be one of them

00:10:25.133 --> 00:10:28.234
and unwind a plot
before it takes place.

00:10:28.234 --> 00:10:30.000
-Right.
-Do you think maybe, perhaps --

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:32.033
and maybe you don't want
to give away your series --

00:10:32.033 --> 00:10:34.167
you find indications
that the FBI

00:10:34.167 --> 00:10:37.000
was actually pushing
for this invasion?

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:48.234
-Earlier today,
the Capitol was under siege

00:10:48.234 --> 00:10:50.033
by people
who can only be described

00:10:50.033 --> 00:10:52.767
as antithetical
to the MAGA movement.

00:10:52.767 --> 00:10:55.133
Now, they were likely
not all Trump supporters

00:10:55.133 --> 00:10:58.267
and there are some reports
that antifa sympathizers

00:10:58.267 --> 00:11:01.033
may have been sprinkled
throughout the crowd.

00:11:01.033 --> 00:11:03.567
-Ah, yes, antifa was "sprinkled
throughout the crowd."

00:11:03.567 --> 00:11:04.801
[ Laughter ]
When you say it like that,

00:11:04.801 --> 00:11:06.667
you make it sound
so warm and cozy.

00:11:06.667 --> 00:11:08.367
Are you describing a riot

00:11:08.367 --> 00:11:09.968
or serving eggnog
at a Christmas party?

00:11:09.968 --> 00:11:11.167
[ Laughter ]
"And, if you notice,

00:11:11.167 --> 00:11:13.000
there's some cinnamon
sprinkled throughout,

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:15.367
just like antifa
at the insurrection."

00:11:15.367 --> 00:11:17.934
[ Laughter ]
We all saw what happened on TV

00:11:17.934 --> 00:11:19.033
with our own eyes that day.

00:11:19.033 --> 00:11:20.601
We even did a live show
that night

00:11:20.601 --> 00:11:23.033
because we didn't know what
the hell was going to happen.

00:11:23.033 --> 00:11:24.567
Had we taped that show
in the afternoon,

00:11:24.567 --> 00:11:26.634
we definitely would've had
to digitally insert

00:11:26.634 --> 00:11:27.767
something like this --

00:11:27.767 --> 00:11:29.901
[Bleep]

00:11:29.901 --> 00:11:32.534
[ Laughter ]

00:11:32.534 --> 00:11:34.901
So, anyway, the point is,
these people all knew

00:11:34.901 --> 00:11:37.100
how dangerous the situation was,

00:11:37.100 --> 00:11:39.934
but in public, since then,
they've defended Trump,

00:11:39.934 --> 00:11:41.601
while downplaying it,
minimizing it,

00:11:41.601 --> 00:11:42.634
or outright lying about it.

00:11:42.634 --> 00:11:43.801
All this answers

00:11:43.801 --> 00:11:46.300
what I like to call
the Costanza question.

00:11:46.300 --> 00:11:48.834
George Costanza, of course,
famously said this --

00:11:48.834 --> 00:11:51.033
-It's not a lie,

00:11:51.033 --> 00:11:52.167
if you believe it.

00:11:52.167 --> 00:11:54.234
[ Laughter ]
-But they didn't believe it.

00:11:54.234 --> 00:11:57.968
Their texts show they were lying
and they knew they were lying,

00:11:57.968 --> 00:12:01.400
which means they're worse
than George Costanza.

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:03.267
That's right -- they're Newman.

00:12:03.267 --> 00:12:04.934
[ Laughter ]

00:12:04.934 --> 00:12:06.334
Of course,
if Congress got its hands

00:12:06.334 --> 00:12:08.100
on George's texts,
he'd freak out, too.

00:12:08.100 --> 00:12:09.734
[ As Costanza ]
Jerry, they got my texts!

00:12:09.734 --> 00:12:10.801
[ As Seinfeld ]
You were texting?

00:12:10.801 --> 00:12:12.133
[ As Costanza ]
I was tapping and typing

00:12:12.133 --> 00:12:13.567
and jiffing and riffing, baby!

00:12:13.567 --> 00:12:15.367
[ As Seinfeld ]
Well, you jiffed and you riffed

00:12:15.367 --> 00:12:16.801
and, now, they're miffed.

00:12:16.801 --> 00:12:18.701
[ "Seinfeld" theme sting ]

00:12:18.701 --> 00:12:19.767
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:12:19.767 --> 00:12:21.567
This latest bombshell
is so revealing,

00:12:21.567 --> 00:12:23.067
in so many ways.
For one thing,

00:12:23.067 --> 00:12:24.801
Trump's closest allies
were pleading with him

00:12:24.801 --> 00:12:26.601
to put a stop to the violence,
and he refused.

00:12:26.601 --> 00:12:29.701
For another, they were honest
in private about how bad it was,

00:12:29.701 --> 00:12:31.067
while, in public,
defending Trump

00:12:31.067 --> 00:12:32.267
and lying about what happened.

00:12:32.267 --> 00:12:34.901
And they're also the ones
who spread the big lie

00:12:34.901 --> 00:12:36.834
about the supposedly stolen
election, to begin with.

00:12:36.834 --> 00:12:40.267
To borrow a phrase, Republicans,
if you had a conscience at all,

00:12:40.267 --> 00:12:41.667
you'd see all the evidence
and...

00:12:41.667 --> 00:12:44.534
-"Condemn this [bleep] asap."

00:12:44.534 --> 00:12:47.000
[ Laughter and applause ]
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:50.167
♪♪

